[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://sim/data/help_page_def.gd" id="1"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1")
id = "citizens_food"
order = 3
title = "Citizens and food"
body = "Each citizen eats {growth.food_per_citizen} food a day. Food made beyond that fills the growth bar. When the bar is full and a bed is free, a new citizen arrives at the Hearth.

Beds come from homes. The Hearth houses {building.hearth.housing_beds}, a Tent {building.tent.housing_beds}, a Cottage {building.cottage.housing_beds}. A citizen without a bed is homeless: Spirit falls and growth stops.

If Spirit is {growth.immigration_spirit} or more and a bed is free, a newcomer also arrives every {growth.immigration_days} days.

If food runs out, {growth.leave_per_day} citizen leaves each day until the food balances.

Citizens with no job take free job slots on their own, in this order: food, water, Lumen, hauling, building, Wood and Stone, refined goods, gold, then the rest. You can set one building to high, normal or low priority, or pause it. You never choose people.

Eating more than one kind of food raises Spirit."
